          %title Contents
          %blockquote
            %p
              this entry is one chapter of “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"}> geometry of physics
              ”
            %p
              previous chapter:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+manifolds+and+orbifolds"} manifolds and orbifolds
            %p
              next chapter:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+BPS+charges"} BPS charges
            %p
              Presently this entry is under construction. It is being incrementally expanded as this lecture series progresses:
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/From+the+Superpoint+to+T-Folds"} From the Superpoint to T-Folds
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Superalgebra"} Superalgebra
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Supergeometry"} Supergeometry
              %li
                %a{:href => "#spacetime_supersymmetry"} Spacetime supersymmetry
              %li
                %a{:href => "#fundamental_super_branes"}
                  Fundamental super
                  = succeed "-branes" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#GeneralReading"} General accounts
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#MoreDetails"} More specialized literature
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesHigherSuperCartan"} Higher super Cartan geometry
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometry"} Klein geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            the fundamental geometric concept is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+group"} symmetry group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            of the local model
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            are reflected in their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+representations"} categories of representations
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(G)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+categories"} tensor categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wigner+classification"} Wigner classification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+objects"} irreducible objects
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(G)
            label the possible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particle"} fundamental particle
            species on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(G)
            as the actual fundamental concept, then the natural question is that of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka reconstruction
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(G)
            for some symmetry group
            = succeed "?" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigid+monoidal+category"} rigid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+categories"} tensor categories
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            subject only to a mild size constraint this is answered by
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne%27s+theorem+on+tensor+categories"} Deligne's theorem on tensor categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to be a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"}> supergroup
            ”. This we discuss in the first section
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Superalgebra"} below
