          %h2#references References
          %p The following first mentions
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#GeneralReading"} General accounts
          %p that might usefully be held on to during the seminar. Then I list
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#MoreDetails"} Special literature
          %p with refernces to original results and to reviews of these. Then I list pointers to my own work with collaborators on
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesHigherSuperCartan"} Higher super Cartan geometry
          %h3#GeneralReading General accounts
          %p An excellent general textbook for our purposes is
          %ul
            %li#CDF
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supergravity+and+Superstrings+-+A+Geometric+Perspective"} Supergravity and Superstrings - A Geometric Perspective
          %p
            This is written by physicists in physics style, but the development is careful and thorough, and the “geometric perspective” in the title is nothing but the perspective of higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartan+geometry"} super Cartan geometry
            in slight disguise. See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
          %p Lecture notes closely related to the seminar are in
          %ul
            %li#StructureTheory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Structure+Theory+for+Higher+WZW+Terms"} Structure Theory for Higher WZW Terms
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.esi.ac.at/activities/events/2015/higher-structures-in-string-theory-and-quantum-field-theory"} Higher Structures in String Theory and Quantum Field Theory
          %h3#MoreDetails More specialized literature
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne%27s+theorem+on+tensor+categories"} Deligne's theorem on tensor categories
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Deligne02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Catégorie Tensorielle
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.ias.edu/files/deligne/Tensorielles.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            building on his general work on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannakian+categories"} Tannakian categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat%C3%A9gories+Tannakiennes"} Catégories Tannakiennes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://publications.ias.edu/sites/default/files/60_categoriestanna.pdf"} pdf
          %p A brief survey is in
          %ul
            %li#Ostrik04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ostrik"}> Victor Ostrik
              ,
              %em Tensor categories (after P. Deligne)
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0401347"}> arXiv:math/0401347
              )
          %p and a more comprehensive texbook account is in chapter 9.11 of
          %ul
            %li#EGNO15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"}> Pavel Etingof
              , Shlomo Gelaki, Dmitri Nikshych,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ostrik"} Victor Ostrik
              = succeed "," do
                %em Tensor categories
              %p ))
          %p
            The observation that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            is naturally regarded as ordinary geometry inside the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoints"} superpoints
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Schwarz84
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"}> Albert Schwarz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the definition of superspace
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/links/b12306f831b8c37d32d5ba8511d60c93/tmf5111.pdf"} russian original pdf
            %li#KonechnySchwarz97
              %p
                Anatoly Konechny,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"} Albert Schwarz
                %em
                  On
                  = succeed "-dimensional" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi k
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi l
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k \oplus l|q)
                in
                %em Supersymmetry and Quantum Field Theory
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Volkov"} Dmitry Volkov
                memorial volume) Springer-Verlag, 1998, Lecture Notes in Physics, 509 , J. Wess and V. Akulov (editors)(
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9706003"}> arXiv:hep-th/9706003
                )
              %p
                %em
                  Theory of
                  = succeed "-dimensional" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi k
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi l
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k \oplus l|q)
                Sel. math., New ser. 6 (2000) 471 - 486
          %p A nice account is in
          %ul
            %li#Sachse08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Sachse"}> Christoph Sachse
              ,
              %em A Categorical Formulation of Superalgebra and Supergeometry
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.4067"}> arXiv:0802.4067
              )
          %p
            Useful discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinors"} Majorana spinors
            and the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            algebras includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#II.7.3"} CDF, II.7.3
            %li#FigueroaOFarrill
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"}> José Figueroa-O'Farrill
                ,
                %em Majorana spinors
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~jmf/Teaching/Lectures/Majorana.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            The close relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+and+division+algebras"} supersymmetry and division algebras
            was first observed in
          %ul
            %li#KugoTownsend83
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taichiro+Kugo"}> Taichiro Kugo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supersymmetry and the division algebras
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/181889"} spires
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://cds.cern.ch/record/140183/files/198301032.pdf"} pdf
          %p A clean survey is in
          %ul
            %li#BH09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
              = succeed "," do
                %em Division algebras and supersymmetry I
              = succeed "(eds.)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"} Jonathan Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Superstrings, Geometry, Topology, and
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.0551"} arXiv:0909.0551
          %p and the discussion of the spinor bilinear pairings from this perspective is in
          %ul
            %li#BH10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
              = succeed "," do
                %em Division algebras and supersymmetry II
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.3436"} arXiv:1003.34360
          %p
            The seminal analysis of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+of+G-structures"} torsion of G-structures
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Guillemin65
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Guillemin"}> Victor Guillemin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The integrability problem for
                  = succeed "-structures" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1994134"} JSTOR
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+of+G-structures"} torsion of G-structures
            in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supertorsion"}> supertorsion
            ) is in
          %ul
            %li#Lott01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Lott"}> John Lott
              ,
              %em The Geometry of Supergravity Torsion Constraints
              Comm. Math. Phys. 133 (1990), 563–615, (exposition in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0108125"} arXiv:0108125
          %p
            An elegant construction of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartan+geometry"} super Cartan geometry
          %ul
            %li#DAuriaFre82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
              ,
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric Superravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/GeometricSupergravity.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            This is the main original result on which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
            is based, as laid out in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CDF"} CDF
          %p
            The observation that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of bosonic solutions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            are equivalent simply to vanishing of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supertorsion"} supertorsion
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#CandielloLechner93
              %p
                A. Candiello, K. Lechner,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Duality in Supergravity Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9309143"} arXiv:hep-th/9309143
            %li#Howe97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"}> Paul Howe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Weyl Superspace
              %p
                Volume 415, Issue 2, 11 December 1997, Pages 149–155 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9707184"}> arXiv:hep-th/9707184
                )
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fierz+identities"} Fierz identities
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#CDF"} CDF, II.8
          %p
            The classification of the invariant super Lie algebra cocycles on super-Minkowski spacetime, hence that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            without gauge fields on their worldvolume, is due to
          %ul
            %li#AETW87
              Anna Achúcarro,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Evans"} Jonathan Evans
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Wiltshire"} David Wiltshire
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Super
                  = succeed "-Branes" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %strong 198
              (1987) 441 (
              %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/22286?ln=en"}> spire
              )
          %p
            The extension of this classification to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetime"} extended super Minkowski spacetime
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#CAIB99
              %p
                C. Chrysso‌malakos,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"} José de Azcárraga
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+M.+Izquierdo"} José M. Izquierdo
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of branes and extended superspaces
                %strong 567
                (2000) 293-330 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9904137"}> arXiv:hep-th/9904137
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00512-X"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00512-X
            %li#Sakaguchi00
              %p
                Makoto Sakaguchi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em IIB-Branes and New Spacetime Superalgebras
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9909143"} arXiv:hep-th/9909143
          %p
            The M5-brane cocycle on the “M2-brane extended super-Minkowski spacetime” that appears here has in fact been observed, as a cocycle, all the way back in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82"} D’Auria-Fré 82
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+WZW+term"} higher WZW term
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz type action functional
            that defines the fundamental
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            has been argued in
          %ul
            %li#BLNPST97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kurt+Lechner"} Kurt Lechner
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Pasti"} Paolo Pasti
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"} Dmitri Sorokin
              = succeed "," do
                %em Covariant Action for the Super-Five-Brane of M-Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9701149"} arXiv:hep-th/9701149
          %p
            The observation that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            on curved
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetimes"} super spacetimes
            require
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalization+of+WZW+term"} definite globalization
            of super Lie algebra cocycles from Minkowski spacetime over the supermanifold is due to
          %ul
            %li#BergshoeffSezginTownsend86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Superstring actions in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 3
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 4
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 6
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 10
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 3, 4, 6, 10
                    curved superspace
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/223138/?ln=en"} spire
            %li#BergshoeffSezginTownsend87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supermembranes and eleven dimensional supergravity
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"} The World in Eleven Dimensions
                69-72 (
                %a{:href => "http://streaming.ictp.trieste.it/preprints/P/87/010.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/248230?ln=en"} spire
          %p
            The formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} topological T-duality
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#BouwknegtEvslinMathai04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Bouwknegt"}> Peter Bouwknegt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jarah+Evslin"} Jarah Evslin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"} Varghese Mathai
              = succeed "," do
                %em T-Duality: Topology Change from H-flux
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0306062"} hep-th/0306062
          %p and in an alternative form due to
          %ul
            %li#BunkeRumpfSchick08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              , P. Rumpf,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schick"} Thomas Schick
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The topology of
                  = succeed "-duality" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  = succeed "-bundles" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi T
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^n
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.GT/0501487"} arXiv:math.GT/0501487
          %p
            The suggestion that there ought to be “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-folds"}> T-folds
            ” or “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+field+theory"}> doubled geometry
            ” is due to
          %ul
            %li#Hull04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"}> Chris Hull
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Geometry for Non-Geometric String Backgrounds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0406102"} arXiv:hep-th/0406102
            %li#Hull06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"}> Chris Hull
                ,
                %em Doubled geometry and T-folds
                JHEP0707:080,2007 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605149"}> arXiv:hep-th/0605149
                )
          %p
            The mathematical formalization of this idea in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundles"} principal 2-bundles
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality+2-group"} T-duality 2-group
            was claimed in
          %ul
            %li#Nikolaus14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em T-Duality in K-theory and elliptic cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %em String Geometry Network Meeting
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ingvet.kau.se/juerfuch/conf/esi14/esi14_34.html"} website
          %h3#ReferencesHigherSuperCartan Higher super Cartan geometry
          %p The following articles develop the higher super Cartan geometry that we give an exposition of in the second part of the seminar.
          %p The mathematical foundation of higher supergeometry:
          %ul
            %li#dcct
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930v1"} v1 arXiv:1310.7930
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/12630719/dcct.pdf"} v2
          %p
            The general idea of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} The brane bouquet
            and the general construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+WZW+terms"} higher WZW terms
            from higher
            = succeed "-cocycles:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %ul
            %li#FSS13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
              International Journal of Geometric Methods in Modern Physics Volume 12, Issue 02 (2015) 1550018, (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5264"}> arXiv:1308.5264
              )
          %p
            The homotopy-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            cocycle and of the type IIA
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            cocycles:
          %ul
            %li#FSS16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Rational+sphere+valued+supercocycles+in+M-theory"} Rational sphere valued supercocycles in M-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03206"} arXiv:1606.03206
          %p
            The derivation of supersymmetric
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} topological T-duality
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+T-folds"} super T-folds
